.TH UUIDGEN 1 2026-10-19 "w64devkit" "w64devkit Manual"
.SH NAME
uuidgen \- generate UUIDs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uuidgen
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-i " | " \-s ]
.RB [ \-n\c
.IR count ]
.RB [ \-o\c
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-x ]
.br
.B uuidgen
.BR \-h " | " \-? " | " \-v
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uuidgen
prints random UUIDs, one per line, or each inside an IDL interface
template or a C structure initializer.
It is a replacement for the
.B uuidgen
in the Windows SDK, with the same options, for use with
.BR widl .
.PP
The UUIDs are version 4.
They come from encrypting a counter with the Speck128/128 cipher, keyed
from the system's random number generator, or from the time and the
program's load address if that fails.
UUIDs from one run are always distinct.
.PP
Output lines end with CRLF, as with the Windows SDK tool.
.SH OPTIONS
An option begins with
.B \-
or
.BR / ,
and only its first letter is significant.
The arguments of
.B \-n
and
.B \-o
must be attached:
.BR \-n5 ,
not
.BR "\-n 5" .
.TP
.B \-c
Use uppercase hex digits.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-?
Print the version and a usage message on standard output, and exit.
.TP
.B \-i
Write each UUID inside an IDL interface template:
.RS
.PP
.EX
[
uuid(a59e8a26\-3f50\-4c24\-a8a7\-6bdae8d7a43f),
version(1.0)
]
interface INTERFACENAME
{
\&
}
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI \-n count
Generate
.I count
UUIDs instead of 1.
.I count
is one or more decimal digits, optionally after a
.BR + ,
and anything after the digits is ignored.
A count of 0 generates nothing, and a count too large to represent
behaves as unlimited.
.TP
.BI \-o path
Write to
.I path
instead of standard output, replacing its contents.
.TP
.B \-s
Write each UUID as a C structure initializer:
.RS
.PP
.EX
INTERFACENAME = { /* a59e8a26\-3f50\-4c24\-a8a7\-6bdae8d7a43f */
    0xa59e8a26,
    0x3f50,
    0x4c24,
    {0xa8, 0xa7, 0x6b, 0xda, 0xe8, 0xd7, 0xa4, 0x3f}
  };
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-x
Ignored.
The Windows SDK tool generates sequential UUIDs with this option.
.PP
When both
.B \-i
and
.B \-s
are given, the last one wins.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid option or count, the output file could not be opened, or an
error writing output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a UUID:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ uuidgen
d48b415d\-86a0\-4ed5\-bb8f\-07bd46e89b2e
.EE
.RE
.PP
Generate three uppercase UUIDs without carriage returns:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ uuidgen \-c \-n3 | tr \-d \(aq\er\(aq
.EE
.RE
.PP
Start a new IDL file:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ uuidgen \-i \-ofoo.idl
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
This is not the util-linux
.BR uuidgen ,
and has none of its options.
Unlike the Windows SDK tool, it accepts a count of 0, and paths may
contain any Unicode characters and be longer than
.BR MAX_PATH .
.PP
The kit also installs this program under target-prefixed names, such as
.BR x86_64\-w64\-mingw32\-uuidgen .
